<p>(a) In the second quarter of 1996, the Company recorded a non-recurring reorganization charge of $3.6 million ($2.1 million, or $0.05 per share, on an after tax basis) in conjunction with the Company's initial public offering on August 7, 1996.</p>
<p>(b) Pro forma adjustments include the elimination of certain expenses in connection with the public offering and include a provision for income taxes at a 40 percent rate as prior to its initial public offering, the Company was an &quot;S&quot; corporation and did not pay full corporate income taxes.</p>
<p>(c) Earnings per share amounts are calculated using 42,682,000 shares, whereby all of the shares outstanding following the Company's public offering are considered to be outstanding for all periods presented.</p>
